cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Analytic First-Order J2 Corrections to the Two-Body Admissible-Region Boundary"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
type: software
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
abstract: "Python source and verification scripts for closed-form, first-order J2 perturbation corrections to the energy and perigee boundary curves of the admissible-region method for too-short-arc initial orbit determination. Symbolic identities are checked with SymPy residuals; numerical claims are reproduced by RK45 integration of the J2-perturbed equations of motion."
authors:
  - given-names: Praise
    family-names: Nesvinga
    affiliation: "National University of Science and Technology, Bulawayo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-3518-8963"
keywords:
  - orbit determination
  - admissible region
  - too-short arc
  - J2 perturbation
  - space situational awareness

